  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f$ be a real valued function on $\\mathbb R$ such that $f$ is twice differentiable. Suppose that $f\\prime$ vanishes only at $0$ and $f\\doubleprime$ is everywhere negative. Define a function $h$ by $h(x)=(x-a)^2-f(x)$, where $a>0$. Then",
  "options": {
    "A": "$h$ has a local minima in $(0,a)$;",
    "B": "$h$ has a local maxima in $(0,a)$;",
    "C": "$h$ is monotonically increasing in $(0,a)$;",
    "D": "$h$ is monotonically decreasing in $(0,a)$"
  },
  "answer": "A",
